Derive the following Gibbs Free Energy and Constant-Temperature, Constant-Pressure Processes relation from the preceding result, showing the algebra, calculus, counting, or thermodynamic identity used at each step.
\[
\begin{aligned}
dG&=dU+p\,dV-T\,dS\\
&=\delta Q-\delta W_{\mathrm{non}}-T\,dS\\
&\le-\delta W_{\mathrm{non}}.
\end{aligned}
\tag*{[3]}
\]
Notation: \(G,H,U,S,T,p,V\) denotes Gibbs free energy, enthalpy, internal energy, entropy, absolute temperature, pressure, and total volume; unit \(\mathrm{J, J, J, J K^{-1}, K, Pa, m^{3}}\); \(\delta Q,\delta W_{\mathrm{non}},\delta W\) denotes heat into the system, non-expansion work by the system, and total work by the system; unit \(\mathrm{J, J, J}\); \(\Delta G,\Delta H,\Delta S,W_{\mathrm{non,max}}\) denotes finite Gibbs, enthalpy, and entropy changes and maximum non-expansion work; unit \(\mathrm{J, J, J K^{-1}, J}\); \(\Delta G_m,\Delta H_m,\Delta S_m\) denotes molar Gibbs, enthalpy, and entropy changes; unit \(\mathrm{J mol^{-1}, J mol^{-1}, J mol^{-1} K^{-1}}\).

